## Building in quality

We build quality in as we go, rather than checking for it at the end.

* **Automated tests and CI**: we add or update tests alongside our changes and
  do not merge while CI checks are failing.
* **Documentation alongside code**: if a change affects how something is
  built, run or used, we update the documentation in the same piece of work.
* **Security and data protection by default**: we think about access, secrets,
  encryption and personal data from the start, and keep credentials out of
  code, pull requests, logs and Slack.
* **Decisions in the open**: we discuss significant decisions openly, then
  record them as
  [architecture decision records](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/integration-hub/tree/main/architecture-decision-record)
  so the reasoning stays visible.

## Ceremonies

We work in fortnightly cycles. Our ceremonies give us regular time together to
agree priorities, make progress visible and improve how we work.

| Ceremony | Occurrence | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Stand-up | Monday to Thursday | Catch up, share progress and blockers, and agree who needs to talk afterwards. |
| Backlog refinement | Fortnightly | Talk through upcoming work together so it is clear enough to plan. |
| Planning | Fortnightly | Agree what we will focus on over the next fortnight. |
| Retrospective | Last Friday | Reflect on how we have worked together, celebrate what went well and choose something to improve. |
| Show and tell | Last Thursday | Share our progress and learning with colleagues and stakeholders. |

Stand-up is for coordinating, not for proving how busy we are. Keep updates
short and pick up detailed problem-solving afterwards with the people who need
to be involved.

Before refinement, look at the work likely to come up and bring your
questions. Work is ready to plan when we understand the outcome, the important
risks and what needs to be true for it to be done.

Retrospectives are a safe space to talk honestly about how we work: what is
going well, what is getting in the way and what we would like to try next. We
follow up on the actions we agree.

Show and tell is where we share our work openly. Anyone interested is welcome,
and it is a good moment to recognise what we have achieved together.

## Changing how we work

This page belongs to all of us. If something here stops helping, bring it to a
retrospective or raise a pull request to change it.